\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces UMAP of mean$(S)$ (left) and $\mathrm  {concat}(P)$ (right) coloured by PAM50 subtype for the methods emphasised in this thesis (MOCSS, Method~1, Method~1+VICReg, Method~2, Method~3, OMIDIENT). Focus on those rows; any additional Method~4 row that may appear in the panel is outside the scope of this thesis and should be ignored. MOCSS private embeddings retain strong subtype structure; Method~2 shows structured but differently organised layouts on both sides; Method~3 preserves competitive shared geometry; OMIDIENT private embeddings lack subtype organisation consistent with collapse.}}{33}{figure.caption.32}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:umap}{{10}{33}{UMAP of mean$(S)$ (left) and $\mathrm {concat}(P)$ (right) coloured by PAM50 subtype for the methods emphasised in this thesis (MOCSS, Method~1, Method~1+VICReg, Method~2, Method~3, OMIDIENT). Focus on those rows; any additional Method~4 row that may appear in the panel is outside the scope of this thesis and should be ignored. MOCSS private embeddings retain strong subtype structure; Method~2 shows structured but differently organised layouts on both sides; Method~3 preserves competitive shared geometry; OMIDIENT private embeddings lack subtype organisation consistent with collapse}{figure.caption.32}{}}
